      'Setup example: 9 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Your team wins the point if one of you takes more tricks than any other single player; if tied, the first to have reached that trick count wins the point for the team.',
      'Turn-flow example: Left of dealer leads; no suit obligation. Highest card wins trick (ties = trick spoiled, same player leads again). Nine tricks. First to 3 tricks turns a card face up; first to 3 turns two up (to remember order for ties). Partners may signal by agreed gestures.',
      'Scoring example: Team of the individual with most tricks (or first to that count) gets 1 point. Match = 5 deals; higher total wins. Mordienne: win with a run of consecutive tricks at the end after none earlier = 2 points. Surrender possible; refusal commits opponents to mordienne or give 2 to surrendering team. Your team wins the point if one of you takes more tricks than any other single player; if tied, the first to have reached that trick count wins the point for the team..',
